    "description": "Chinese Cloisonne Desk Stand & Chopsticks Lot\nCloisonne Enamel & Camel Bone Desk & Dining Collectibles\nVintage, Beijing 1991\nThis vintage Chinese decorative lot includes a brass and cloisonne enamel double pen stand with a center lidded inkwell box, paired with a boxed set of four pairs of camel bone chopsticks with matching blue floral cloisonne handles. Purchased in Beijing in 1991, both items showcase traditional wirework with vibrant floral and scroll motifs on a cobalt ground.\nItems Included:\nCloisonne Double Pen Stand: Features two swivel pen sockets and a central lidded compartment with turquoise enameled interior; measures approximately 7.25 inches wide.\nBoxed Chopstick Set: Four pairs (8 total) of camel bone chopsticks with cloisonne handles in a patterned brocade fabric case with bone toggles and internal provenance note.\nCondition:\nCloisonne enamel remains vibrant and intact with minimal wear. Metal borders show light patina. Brocade storage box has minor handling wear with intact clasps.",
